                <pb facs="0812" n="1320" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/8–1848</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of United
                        Nations Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rusk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-08-18">August 18, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Deterioration in Palestine Situation</p>
                <p>Your attention is invited urgently to Mr. Douglas’s telegram 3732 of August 17,
                    reporting Bevin’s very serious concern over the Palestine situation and his hope
                    that this government will be able to take immediate and forceful steps with the
                    Provisional Government of Israel to halt Jewish aggression. You will note that
                    Bevin requests an answer by today, the 18th.</p>
                <p>Mr. Douglas’s telegram underscores the need for action pursuant to the memorandum
                    to the President which was submitted by the Secretary to the White House on
                    August 16. I venture to suggest, therefore, that you or the Secretary inquire of
                    the President his reaction to this memorandum, particularly in light of
                    Ambassador Douglas’s telegram of yesterday.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d538-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Copies of these documents are attached.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
